			<div class="content" id="post-content-1865506">
									

<p><strong>Note: This item has been edited from its deliberately contentious initial form into something a bit more subuded. This was a planned edit and is not due to feedback. Comments made prior to about 0800 EDT on 8 October pertain to the previous version.</strong></p>
<p>Later on when I have more time, I may throw something on the Leaks thread to explain the execution in full, but the tl;dr version is as follows: as Waterfire and a couple of other people realized, a major part of the original version of this skip was intended to be the extension of the 'polarizing' effect to the Wiki voter base. Many aspects of the entry - from the 'lolsupplement' to the way in which the random effect was implemented - were deliberately selected in order to invoke this effect.</p>
<p>I didn't want that version of the article to last forever, so I set its duration to be about 24 hours, figuring that if I failed badly that'd be when it was deleted anyway. As it was, the votes at that time were hovering in the single-digit pluses with about 50 total voters, which was close enough to a polarized vote for me to declare a qualified success. (As I told a couple of people before I posted this, my ideal result would have been an average of 0 after 24 hours with 100 votes or more.)</p>
<p><em>PS: I'm only replying here because I wasn't quick enough to get the first post on my own thread. D'oh!</em></p>
<p>EDIT: If anyone wants to see the 'anomalously defaced' page that could be found from one of the prior iterations, it can be found on the sandbox <a href="http://scpsandbox2.wikidot.com/mrcarbon:page3">here</a>. <strong>Please note that this is no longer part of this article!</strong> I provide it simply so that those who didn't catch the time-limited original version can still see the <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">eye damage</span> wonderful artistic statement.</p>

							</div>

								
